msgstr "詳細な例については :doc:`templates` を参照してください。"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:130
msgid "Math Rendering"
msgstr "数式のレンダリング"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:133
msgid "mitex Support"
msgstr "mitexサポート"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:135
msgid "Enable LaTeX math rendering with mitex:"
msgstr "mitexを使用してLaTeX数式レンダリングを有効化します："

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:141
msgid ""
"When enabled, LaTeX math expressions are converted to Typst using the "
"mitex package. When disabled, math is passed directly as Typst math "
"syntax."
msgstr "有効にすると、LaTeX数式はmitexパッケージを使用してTypstに変換されます。無効にすると、数式はTypstの数式構文として直接渡されます。"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:145
msgid "Author Information"
msgstr "著者情報"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:148
msgid "Detailed Format"
msgstr "詳細な形式"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:150
msgid "Include detailed author information:"
msgstr "詳細な著者情報を含めます："

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:168
msgid "Paper Size and Format"
msgstr "用紙サイズとフォーマット"

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:174
msgid ""
"``papersize`` and ``fontsize`` set the paper size and the base font size."
" ``typst_elements`` supports three keys in total; the third, ``lang``, is"
" documented in `Document Language`_ below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:179
msgid "Document Language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:181
msgid ""
"The ``lang`` key controls the language Typst uses when generating its own"
" labels -- most notably the figure and table supplement text (for example"
" \"Figure\" / \"Table\" in English). It is passed through to the "
"template's ``project()`` function and reaches Typst's text setup. The "
"effect is concrete: with a Japanese setting, a captioned table renders as"
" 「表 1」 and a figure as 「図 1」, where the default English setting renders "
"\"Table 1\" and \"Figure 1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:190
msgid "Automatic derivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:192
msgid ""
"When your project uses the bundled default template, ``lang`` is derived "
"automatically from Sphinx's own ``language`` setting -- no explicit "
"configuration is needed. The derivation rule is simple: take the part of "
"the value before the first underscore, hyphen, or at-sign, and lowercase "
"it. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:198
msgid "``ja`` becomes ``ja``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:199
msgid "``zh_CN`` becomes ``zh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:200
msgid "``pt_BR`` becomes ``pt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:202
msgid ""
"If a ``language`` value cannot be reduced to a two- or three-letter code,"
" typsphinx emits a build warning naming the value and leaves the "
"parameter unset, so the template's own default applies and the build "
"still succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:208
msgid "Scope: default template only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:210
msgid ""
"Automatic derivation applies **only** when the bundled default template "
"is what actually gets used. It does **not** apply when ``typst_template``"
" is configured, when ``typst_package`` is configured, or when a file "
"named ``base.typ`` sits next to your ``conf.py`` in the source directory "
"(which silently shadows the bundled template). The reason: a template "
"that does not declare a ``lang`` parameter would receive an argument it "
"never asked for, and Typst aborts the compile on an undeclared argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:218
msgid ""
"If you use a custom template or package and want the same behavior, opt "
"in explicitly: declare a ``lang`` parameter in your own ``project()`` (or"
" equivalent entry function) and then set it through ``typst_elements``, "
"as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:224
msgid "Precedence and known limitation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:226
msgid ""
"An explicit ``typst_elements`` ``lang`` entry always wins over the value "
"derived from ``language``, on every template path, and an explicit value "
"is passed through to Typst exactly as written with no validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:235
msgid ""
"Here the derived value would be ``ja``, but the explicit entry wins, so "
"Typst typesets in German and renders 「Tabelle 1」."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/configuration.rst:238
msgid ""
"**Known limitation:** region subtags are not supported, so a ``zh_TW`` "
"project resolves to ``zh`` and renders simplified-Chinese supplement text"
" 「图 1」 rather than the traditional 「圖 1」. If you need traditional "
"Chinese, set the value explicitly through your own template."
msgstr ""

